# secret_guard.sh allow-list — one glob per line (matched against the repo path).
# Allow-listed hits are still REPORTED ("ALLOWED") but do not block commits/merges/pushes.
#
# .env.example is a template. It must contain placeholders only.
# Encryption keys and real .env files are not allow-listed.
# A blob already on main may ride along in a merge (the guard allows an unchanged
# parent blob). A new commit that adds or changes a key still fails.
# The env may hold only the primary key for the initial DB password. Other keys
# belong in the database, not in git.
.env.example
